  "authorization": "Standing source-preserving complete ash-helper and collection approvals, existing independently inspected Swiss slag component review, approved copper water proxies and nonphysical waste-indicator policy. No new disposal fate, incineration, recovery credit, allocation assumption or reverse route.",
  "limitations": "Exact Swiss copper bottom-ash disposal reconstruction, after municipal incineration FAE. Preserve the source copper-specific physical releases and their signed kg quantities, separate one-kg operating service and original facility fraction. Reuse only independently reviewed Swiss slag operation/facility proxies with their heat, energy, water, freight and vintage warnings. Retain both original market collection modes and quantities through existing exact-profile complete freight mappings. No copper incineration, metal recovery credit, horse-dung ash, concrete disposal, moisture scaling or generic ash composition is added. Preserve source uncertainty, pedigree and formulas on reconstructed links. Native water proxies retain signed kg, long-term groundwater and explicit surface-water-to-unspecified receiving-water warnings. Retain exact nonphysical waste inventory indicators where supported; otherwise use only the already approved indicator omission with warnings. Physical copper releases may not be omitted. Caller sign reversal is factor -1 for the negative reference; preserve caller-owned metadata, uncertainty, formulas, foreground suppliers and separate emissions. Only inspected 3.11 and 3.12 cut-off profiles; no inverse is inferred. This review does not resolve the distinct copper-FAE or reused-energy allocation boundaries.",
